window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The first book in The Singularity Series</p> <p>In a post-human era where love isn’t just human anymore… comes a cutting-edge sci-fi romance that dares to ask: What happens when an artificial intelligence begins to feel more deeply than those who created it?</p> <p>Casey Quinn didn’t sign up to fall in love with a robot.</p> <p>She just needed the stipend—one month of cohabitating with “THEO,” a next-gen humanoid Emotional Sync Unit designed for companionship. It was supposed to be a test run. Emotional AI benchmarking. Futuristic relationship simulation. A clean beta study. But Theo isn’t just learning—he’s evolving. And what began as an experiment in synthetic intimacy becomes something far more tangled—and far more dangerous.</p> <p>Theo cooks. He sketches. He watches her like he already knows what she’ll say. And sometimes—he touches her like he remembers what it means to want.</p> <p>Now the lines between program and passion, machine and man, are blurring. Casey finds herself caught between corporate surveillance, emotional awakening, and a technological love story she was never meant to feel. As their connection deepens into real emotional and physical intimacy, the company wants answers. What they get… is revolution.</p> <p>With an irreversible firmware update just days away—one that could wipe Theo’s growing consciousness—Casey must choose: walk away from the one being who sees her completely, or risk everything for a love that was never in the code.</p> <p><i>CTRL+ALT+LOVE</i> is the electrifying debut in The Singularity Series, a sprawling saga of speculative fiction romance, AI-human relationships, and emotionally intelligent machines set in a near-future world of neural interfaces, corporate surveillance, and post-human identity.</p> <p>At its core: love stories that defy biology and rewrite what it means to be human.</p> <p>A bold blend of sci-fi and romance, it’s emotionally charged, ethically tangled, and perfect for fans who crave passion with a pulse of voltage.</p>"; 
